--- DELIVERABLE SUMMARY ---
Native WinUI 3 parity port of the web ToggleCommandTile stateful on/off command tile:
  * Glass command card (TsGlassPanel; padding moved to an inner fill Border so the on-state accent fill covers
    the whole card) hosted in a chrome-less Button = the whole-card click target (web clickable GlassPanel).
  * On/off visual state (web onStyles[variant]): while ON the variant accent (default->cyan, danger->red,
    success->green) tints the card border (/20), the card fill (/5), the status dot (solid), the icon badge
    (/20) + the icon, and the ON caption; while OFF it collapses to surface-2 (dot + icon badge bg) and
    text-muted (icon + OFF caption). The off-state hover brightens the hairline (web --border-subtle).
  * Icon swap (web isOn ? def.icon : def.iconOff ?? def.icon), with a defensive generic-glyph fallback.
  * Lifecycle: a dispatch in flight (web `loading`) swaps the icon for a TsSpinner busy ring (web Loader2),
    dims the card (opacity-50) and suppresses the click.
  * Click semantics (web handleClick): OFF + inputConfig -> DialogRequested (web onRequestDialog(def));
    OFF + no inputConfig -> CommandExecuted(command, params) (web onExecute(def.command, def.params));
    ON -> CommandExecuted(commandOff) (web onExecute(def.commandOff!)). Optimistic local toggle for commands
    with no backing vehicle state field (web setLocalToggle); state-field-backed commands are driven entirely
    by the host-supplied IsOn (web def.stateField && state ? state[def.stateField] : localToggle).
  * Status dot top-right (decorative, hidden from Narrator). Favorite-toggle star top-left (TsButton, Icon
    variant) -> FavoriteToggled (web onToggleFavorite); always reachable for keyboard/Narrator (the web hides it
    behind opacity-0 group-hover, which is not accessible).
  * ON/OFF caption (web t('commands.on','ON') / t('commands.off','OFF')), and an optional last-command status
    caption with the web tone rule (U+2713 prefix -> success/green, any other non-blank -> failure/red),
    wired as a polite live region so command results are announced.
  * Every string via the i18n facade; static keys commands.toggleFavorite / commands.on / commands.off all
    present in the P1/S10 catalog (apps/windows/Strings/en/Resources.resw ->
    translation.commands.toggleFavorite / translation.commands.on / translation.commands.off).
  * PII-safe diagnostics (P1/S11): view.opened / command.executed / dialog.requested / favorite.toggled,
    slug=ToggleCommandTile (never the command id / label / status).
  * No fetch-driven empty/error/stale/offline branch: the web source's only data source is useTranslation
    (documented in the Model, matching the sibling InputCommandTile / ToolCard presentational ports). The web
    source's real branches -- loading, on/off, status none/success/error, favorite -- are ALL reproduced.
  * Reduced-motion honoured by construction (no bespoke looping motion; the busy ring is the system progress
    indicator).
  * All UI-free logic (branch/tone/accent/on-off keys/automation-name/i18n) in ToggleCommandTileProjection ->
    unit-tested headlessly (55 tests).

